WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:09.640
JaQuel Knight is the creative mind

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.740
behind many of Beyoncé's
iconic performances.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.690
He's worked with her for years

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.220
and he's been dancing his entire life.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.010
I remember dancing in my
grandmother's living room.

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:23.890
And then when I was 16, I
started my own dance group

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.520
with my best friend in Atlanta.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.790
So that was kinda the first serious step

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.490
towards choreography
and creative direction.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.040
At just 18, JaQuel landed a gig

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:34.873
choreographing

00:00:34.873 --> 00:00:36.913
one of the best videos of all time.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.290
Single Ladies.

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:43.670
Years later, JaQuel reveals what it takes

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:46.100
to be a back-up dancer for Beyonce.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.920
To work for B as a dancer,
it takes everything,

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.050
you know.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.750
She's a southern girl, you know,

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.020
who's worked very hard
to get where she is.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.382
So she want people to do the same.

00:00:56.382 --> 00:00:59.070
She wanna know that
you want it really bad.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:02.210
She wanna see your heart,
your passion, your drive.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:05.360
And then, you know, you
gotta be able to jam.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:06.830
How greasy can you get?

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:09.193
How can you hit it hard?

00:01:10.356 --> 00:01:11.640
Then there's also the side of her

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.390
that's looking for the technical element.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:14.290
You know, are you trained?

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:15.970
Do you have any ballet training?

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.589
Do you have any jazz training?

00:01:17.589 --> 00:01:18.800
How are your lines?

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:19.940
You know, so there's a few things

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:21.570
that go into the process.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:24.170
And once we start to
audition things, you know,

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:25.860
we look for everything.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.390
We teach them hip hop number,

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:29.910
we teach them a super
difficult technical number,

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:32.820
we teach them the classic
Beyoncé number, you know.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.480
And then besides that, you know,

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:38.880
you gotta be able to carry
the stage, you know, with her.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.310
You gotta be able to stand next to her

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.690
and be just as good, you know.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:46.110
And sometimes people are
ready, sometimes they're not.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:47.210
You can be a great dancer,

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:50.523
but it may not come through
when you get on stage.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.590
You may kind of pull into a shell,

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:54.940
don't know who to look at.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:56.960
So she's looking for stars.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:59.678
Star dancers, who have magic.

00:01:59.678 --> 00:02:01.930
That can bring it, you know,

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:04.070
and pull other people in, always.

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:06.770
Working with B during
the rehearsal process

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.960
is like, it's kind of a out
of body experience, ya know.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:14.000
People don't understand
the amount of effort

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.890
her work ethic is out of this world.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:18.870
And it's never just one thing.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:21.430
When we're creating
choreography, it's okay, boom.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.570
Where's the wardrobe at?

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:23.860
You know, bring them in so they can see

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:25.090
what the choreography is.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.110
Okay boom.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:27.210
Where are we on this stage?

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.750
You know, let's make sure lighting knows

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.850
how to light this, boom.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:31.690
Where are the cameras?

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:33.910
Okay, let's look at this
camera and then do this.

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:35.670
You know, we're always thinking

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:38.200
of every single piece of the puzzle.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.350
But you know, at the end of the day,

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:42.060
we send her pictures, we send her videos.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.740
She's watching people in rehearsal

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:44.650
like who's that?

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.330
Okay, that's so and so
that we talked about.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:47.860
She's like okay, she's good.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:50.150
You know, she's looking at everything

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.800
at every moment, you know.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.633
So she's like heavily involved.

